  dict({
    'exit_code': 1,
    'stderr': '',
    'stdout': '''
      Refusing to merge: The same scanner was assigned to more than one shard: bandit (shards 0 and 1).
      Its findings would be counted once per shard.
  
    ''',
  })
# ---
# name: test_refusal[owning_shard_recorded_no_result]
  dict({
    'exit_code': 1,
    'stderr': '',
    'stdout': '''
      Refusing to merge: The shard that owned these scanners recorded no result for them: semgrep (owned
      by shard 1). Another shard's skip marker is the only trace left, and adopting it would report a
      scanner that never ran as deliberately skipped. Check whether that shard's scan phase completed.
  
    ''',
  })
# ---
# name: test_refusal[scanner_in_results_owned_by_no_shard]
  dict({
    'exit_code': 1,
    'stderr': '',
    'stdout': '''
      Refusing to merge: These scanners appear in shard results but no shard was assigned them: trivy
      (PASSED, seen in shard0/ash_aggregated_results.json). No shard ran them, so merging would report
      them as deliberately skipped rather than never attempted. The status of each is named above because
      the cause differs: the executors resolved different scanner sets (one missing a plugin module, or
      --python-only or a config override applied to some jobs and not others), or a scanner was excluded
      by every shard's partition. A scanner that failed to construct, or whose plugin module failed to
      import, is recorded ERROR or MISSING instead and is reported through --fail-on-incomplete-scanners
      rather than refused here.
  
    ''',
  })
# ---
# name: test_refusal[shard_completed_none_of_its_scanners]
  dict({
    'exit_code': 1,
    'stderr': '',
    'stdout': '''
      Refusing to merge: These shards completed none of the scanners they owned:
        shard 1 of 2: semgrep (MISSING)
      Their scanners contributed no findings because they did not run, not because there was nothing to
      find, so merging would report a partial scan as a whole one. Check whether those CI jobs had the
      scanners' tools available. Pass --no-fail-on-incomplete-scanners to merge anyway.
  
    ''',
  })
# ---
