# name: test_refusal[shard_selected_another_shards_scanner]
  dict({
    'exit_code': 1,
    'stderr': '',
    'stdout': '''
      Refusing to merge: These shards intended to run a scanner assigned to another shard: semgrep
      (selected by shard 0, assigned to shard 1). A shard only runs what it was assigned, so the exclusion
      that implements the split did not take effect on that executor -- the scanner ran on both shards and
      its findings would be counted once per shard. The assignments themselves are disjoint, so no other
      check here can see this.
  
    ''',
  })
# ---
# name: test_refusal[unstamped_shard]
  dict({
    'exit_code': 1,
    'stderr': '',
    'stdout': '''
      Refusing to merge: No shard provenance found in 1 results file(s):
        shard0/ash_aggregated_results.json
      Only a scan run with --shard-index and --shard-count records which scanners it owned, and without
      that record there is no way to tell a complete set of shards from a partial one. Refusing to guess:
      an unstamped file could equally be a whole unsharded scan or one shard of many.
  
    ''',
  })
